            make_q("What is the 'learning rate vs number of trees' tradeoff in Gradient Boosting?", ["Lowering learning rate requires fewer trees", "Lowering learning rate requires proportionally more trees to reach convergence, but achieves superior test set generalization", "They are completely independent", "Learning rate has no effect on tree count"], 1, "Shrinkage slows convergence: halving $\\eta$ roughly doubles the required trees, but consistently improves generalization."),
